vaporOS nuttx-apps patch: readline-eof-ctrl-d

Problem:   Ctrl-D does nothing in readline: control bytes are silently dropped, so
           an interactive program (the vlua REPL, any shell) has no way to see
           end-of-file from the keyboard.
Fix:       Ctrl-D (0x04) on an empty line makes readline return 0 (EOF).
Upstream:  YES, likely: standard line-discipline behaviour. Make it
           configurable if maintainers prefer.

diff --git a/system/readline/readline_common.c b/system/readline/readline_common.c
index 0fd3b9396..302d31208 100644
--- a/system/readline/readline_common.c
+++ b/system/readline/readline_common.c
@@ -654,6 +791,14 @@ ssize_t readline_common(FAR struct rl_common_s *vtbl, FAR char *buf,
             }
         }
 
+      /* vaporOS: Ctrl-D on an empty line is end-of-file */
+
+      else if (ch == 0x04 && nch == 0)
+        {
+          buf[0] = '\0';
+          return 0;
+        }
+
       /* Check for the beginning of a VT100 escape sequence */
 
       else if (ch == ASCII_ESC)
